{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa Starts Dating Marco", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What Shall We Get?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe plans for the organization of events.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Will, May, Might", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense (<span class =\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future. You can also use the modals <span class =\"strong\">might</span> and <span class =\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The auxiliary <span class =\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is <span class=\"strong\">'ll</span>.<br /><br />  You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions.<br /><br />  The modals <span class =\"strong\">might</span>   and <span class =\"strong\">may</span>   go before the verb.<br /><br />  They talk about future possibility or chance that something will happen.<br /><br /> <span class =\"strong\">Might</span>   means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%).<br /><br />  <span class =\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'll have just one of those, please. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We might have a few hot dogs left. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We may not have any salted butter though.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Quantifiers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns. You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Quantifier </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br /> less/fewer<br /> no/none<br /> any/not any<br /> some<br /> a lot of/lots of<br /> plenty of<br /> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount<br /> a smaller number/amount<br /> 0<br /> ask about a number or amount/say there is no<br /> a small number/amount<br /> a very large number/amount<br /> more than you need<br /> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "There's plenty of popcorn in there!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't want any butter on it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There is not enough butter on this.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "treat ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a tasty food that you do not get to eat very often ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to buy us some treats from the stand.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear at the movie theater. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "popcorn ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a kind of corn that bursts open when heated ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love to eat popcorn with lots of butter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hot dog ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a cooked sausage in a long piece of bread ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'd like one hot dog please.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "nachos", "type": "name"}, {"content": "tortilla chips covered with cheese", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can I get some nachos please?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "pretzel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a salty type of bread baked in the shape of a loose knot", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Are there any pretzels left?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "licorice", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a long, thick red or black piece of chewy candy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'd also like some licorice please. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "ice cream sandwich", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ice cream between two cookies", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love eating ice cream sandwiches in the summer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "soda", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sweet carbonated drink ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can I get two large sodas please?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go on the Internet or to a supermarket. Find a flyer for a supermarket.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of the food and drinks you see.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What items would you buy?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 7-8 sentences about the items. Start your sentence with <span class=\"italic\">If I go shopping, I will buy ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use 4 quantifiers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read them aloud to your partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write about food and drink.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about the quantities of food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about possible actions in the future.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le09ob06re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le09ob06re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob06re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: There's only ten more minutes before the movie starts. Can you find us two seats? I'll grab treats from the concession stand.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Okay.<br /><span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Can I help you?<br /><span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: Yes, I'd like a large popcorn and a hot dog.<br /><span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Any extra butter with the popcorn?"}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob06re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "16200", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: No butter please. Can I get some nachos? Do you have any more pretzels?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: We may have some left. Oh no, sorry, we're out of pretzels, but we have plenty of pizza.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: All right, then I'll have a slice of pizza.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Will that be all?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: No, I'd like some licorice and an ice cream sandwich."}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob06re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "37500", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Anything to drink?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: Yes, I'll take two large sodas.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: That'll be $54.50.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: What?! That's crazy!<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: If you look at the board, you can see all the prices are there. Do you still want all this?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: Just the sodas and popcorn."}], "coverimg": "engenn5le09ob06re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": "engenn5le09ob06re6aud01", "type": "audio"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "text", "id": 3}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can talk about food and drinks. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can use words to describe general quantities. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about possible actions and events in the future.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What do you like to eat when you go to the movies?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What do you usually get?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " Let's visit the concession stand with Marco!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " Marco is buying treats from the <span class=\"t